---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure | PubMed Trivia"
  description="PubMed Trivia publishes clear disclosures about advertising, affiliate programs, and sponsored content, and explains how editorial independence is protected."
  lang="en"
>
  <article>
    <h1>Advertising and Affiliate Disclosure</h1>

    <p>
      PubMed Trivia keeps access to its medical research summaries free by relying on a mix of
      display advertising and affiliate programs. To preserve reader trust, this page explains
      how we earn revenue, how we label commercial relationships, and how our editorial decisions
      stay independent of those relationships.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Affiliate programs we participate in</h2>
    <p>
      We participate in the following affiliate programs:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Amazon Associates (Amazon.co.jp)</strong>:
        Book and related-product links at the end of our articles may be Amazon Associates
        referral links. If a reader clicks through and makes a purchase, PubMed Trivia may
        receive a small commission from Amazon. Clicking a link does not change the price you
        pay on Amazon in any way.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Moshimo Affiliate (Rakuten Books and others)</strong>:
        Some articles include links to Rakuten Books and other retailers routed through the
        Moshimo affiliate network. The same principle applies: we may earn a commission from
        qualifying purchases, and your price is unaffected.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Third-party display advertising (Google AdSense and others)</h2>
    <p>
      We intend to display advertisements through Google AdSense. Google and other third-party
      vendors use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites.
      You can opt out of personalized advertising at the
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads settings</a>
      page. Additional information about how we handle cookies and advertising data is in our
      <a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Sponsored content and partnerships</h2>
    <p>
      Pharmaceutical companies, medical-device manufacturers, and other health-sector sponsors
      may occasionally commission tie-up content on this site. To keep sponsored content clearly
      distinguishable from our regular editorial coverage, we follow these rules:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A &ldquo;Sponsored&rdquo;, &ldquo;Ad&rdquo;, or &ldquo;Provided by [sponsor name]&rdquo;
          label is placed near the article title and at the top of the article body.</li>
      <li>Any claim made in sponsored content must be supported by a primary study or systematic
          review, which we cite.</li>
      <li>We decline any placement that conflicts with our
          <a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a>, or that promotes claims not
          adequately supported by the published evidence.</li>
      <li>Final editing decisions &mdash; including wording, framing, and structure &mdash; rest
          with the PubMed Trivia editorial team, not the sponsor.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      As of November 2026, no sponsored content has yet been published on this site. Any
      future sponsored posts will follow the rules above.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How we protect editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Advertising and affiliate revenue have no influence on what topics we cover, how we
      summarize studies, or how we interpret evidence. In practical terms:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Topics are chosen based on our editor&rsquo;s expertise and reader demand, not
          commercial considerations.</li>
      <li>Outside of clearly labeled sponsored content, we never recommend specific supplements,
          drugs, or branded products.</li>
      <li>We prioritize systematic reviews and large randomized controlled trials; we do not
          tilt our summaries to favor any advertiser or affiliate partner.</li>
      <li>Amazon Associates links are limited to books and resources mentioned in the article,
          or close variants on the same topic. We do not insert off-topic product links.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Reporting concerns</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this disclosure, or if you notice an ad or affiliate link
      that appears to violate these policies, please get in touch via our
      <a href="/en/contact/">Contact page</a>. We take such reports seriously and will act
      promptly.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Related pages</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/en/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/about/">About PubMed Trivia</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/editor/">Editor profile</a></li>
      <li><a href="/en/contact/">Contact</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      <small>Last updated: 18 November 2026</small>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
